dem-replace-line.gls -- dem-replace-line.txt

The file: one line of 100,000 "NNNNNN foo " (1.1 MB).  It is wrapped at
the window's edge (a line of 64 KB or more is not wrapped at words).

Open:   chezweb dem-replace-line.txt

1. M-% foo RET barbaz RET !
   Expect: "100000 substitutions", and the display after it, within
   0.5 s (the display alone took 188 s before 22 November 2026).
2. C-/                   Expect: the text as it was, within 0.5 s.
3. M-% foo RET x RET !   Expect: within 0.5 s.
4. C-x C-w /tmp/dem-replace-line-x.txt RET
     sed s/foo/x/g dem-replace-line.txt | cmp - /tmp/dem-replace-line-x.txt
   Expect: no output.
5. C-x k RET.
